NS_ :

BS_:

BU_:

BO_ [CAN ID] [MessageName]: [NumBytes] [Sender]
 SG_ [SignalName] : [StartBit]|[Length]@[ByteOrder][ValueType] ([Scale],[Offset]) [[Min]|[Max]] "[Unit]" [Receivers]




++++++++++ EXAMPLES ++++++++++++

VERSION ""

NS_ :

BS_:

BU_:

BO_ 257 MotorStatus: 8 ESP32_Motor
 SG_ Current : 0|16@1- (0.01,0) [-327.68|327.67] "A" Vector__XXX
 SG_ RPM : 16|16@1- (1,0) [-32768|32767] "RPM" Vector__XXX  ** Needs to be divided by 360 deg and 60 sec
 SG_ Temperature : 32|16@1+ (0.1,0) [0|150] "degC" Vector__XXX
 SG_ Position: 48|16@1- (1,0) [-360|360] "deg" Vector__XXX *** Needs to be divided by gear ratio for real output
 SG_ FaultFlag : 54|1@1+ (1,0) [0|1] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ EnabledFlag : 55|1@1+ (1,0) [0|1] "" Vector__XXX

BO_ 258 MotorCommand: 4 ESP32_Reader
 SG_ TargetRPM : 0|16@1- (1,0) [-32768|32767] "RPM" Vector__XXX
 SG_ Enable : 16|1@1+ (1,0) [0|1] "" Vector__XXX

Bo_ 259 

voltage, current, position, speed, some temperatures, maybe pid values, some fault codes
the motor drivers will send 4 temperatures each at 16bit, bus current & voltage at 16bit. these values should be scaled down a lot since we dont need the resolution
this will be at 2hz for now
they will also send positional data at 14bit and 1000hz
the jetson will send positional data at lets assume 14bit for now at 100hz